    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #323\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed to the same branch: `bb/relay-118-agent-runtime-04-08-pause-and-re-wake-thr_trdwtajtuy` (PR #323).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #118: pause and re-wake semantics for Semp's own user conversation, with per-wake `agent_runs` bookkeeping, plus fixes from CI code review.\n\n`SempConversation` (`backend/packages/agent-runtime/src/sempConversation.ts`) is a sibling to issue #229's `DelegationRegistry`, using the same in-memory TTL-reuse pattern but as a singleton (Semprec is single-tenant — one Semp/user conversation, no per-caller key needed) with different TTL-expiry semantics:\n\n- First `send()` wakes a new `agent_runs` row (`triggered_by='user'`, `unit='session'`, `project_item_id` = Semprec's own) and an in-process `AgentSession`.\n- Consecutive `send()` calls within the 24-hour TTL reuse the same session as new turns, without opening a new run.\n- On TTL expiry, the in-memory session is dropped and its wake run finished as `done` — but this only *pauses* the conversation, which has no \"closed\" state; the next `send()`, whenever it arrives, wakes a fresh run.\n- Each wake goes through a `reconstructHistory` port for inheriting prior context; this part ships only an internal stub returning no prior history — #119 will fill it in.\n\nFollow-up commit addressed CI code-review findings on this PR:\n- **High**: fixed a concurrency race in `pause()` — it now claims the entry as `busy` synchronously before its first `await`, so a `send()` arriving mid-pause is rejected instead of reusing a session whose run is concurrently being finished as `done`. Added a regression test.\n- **Medium**: stopped exporting the internal `stubReconstructConversationHistory` default from the package's public index (scope creep beyond what #118 asks for).\n- **Low**: removed an unused `lastActivityAt` field that had no consumer.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `pnpm run build` — all packages compile\n- [x] `pnpm run test:unit` — 83/83 passed\n- [x] `pnpm run test:integration` — 455/455 passed (real ephemeral Postgres), including 10 `SempConversation` tests (race-condition regression test included)\n- [x] `pnpm run test:e2e` — 5/5 passed\n- [x] `pnpm run check:boundaries` — no dependency violations\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
